    "updated_at": "2016-09-08T07:58:40Z",
    "body": "The HTML fragment parsing algorithm is used by e.g. `innerHTML`, i.e. when you parse a fragment rather than a full document. So what you quoted explains this behavior.\n\nThe reason this happens is because before `<svg>` (and `<math>`) in text/html was allowed, some Web pages were using those tags by mistake (or for whatever reason, it had no effect), and also did not include the end tag, so those pages would in the worst case be completely broken when browsers added support for `<svg>` in text/html.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
