    "body": "well, now it is getting more or less clear. But is not it a good time to change this? Those ancient times of HTML/0.1 did pass, now SVG node can have, eg. some JS handler and it can need these removed data, and it knows how to render them in SVG context...\n\n**UPD** [12.4 Parsing HTML fragments](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#html-fragment-parsing-algorithm)\n\n> The following steps form the HTML fragment parsing algorithm. The algorithm takes as input an Element node, referred to as the context element, which gives the context for the parser, as well as input, a **string to parse**, and returns a list of zero or more nodes.\n\nAs I understand, at the moment of calling innerHTML (outerHTML) we have already entire DOM built, so why you do refer fragments parsing in the context of innerHTML, pls explain\n",
