    "body": "aha, sorry forgot about the fact the innerHTML is read/write, not only read\n\nWrt 'no any interest at this point', I noticed that there is DIV start tag in that list of HTML Standard.\n\nBut if look into [SVG2 draft](https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG2/struct.html#UnknownElement), we can notice an example there, and there is a `<div />` inside of it, and we see a remark\n\n> regardless of whether the user agent supports XHTML or not, the ‘div’ element and its contents must not render\n\nand a part of the example\n\n> ``` xml\n> ...\n>  </linearGradient>\n>  <div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">this must not be visible</div>\n> </svg>\n> ```\n\nMust not be visible not means must not be there. But as per HTML standard, DIV tag is just impossible there. It is about 'wrong time to change'. It is very right time to change IMHO\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
